                {
                    "id": "persist-device-bound-login-sessions",
                    "title": "Issue and persist one server-generated device token on the first well-formed request to the existing login, signup, or forgot-password endpoint even when authentication fails or the email is unknown; reuse it on later requests, record the observed IP, guard against mass anonymous device creation, and create a device-bound session only after successful login without adding routes",
                    "version": "0.3.7",
                    "type": "backend",
                    "changeType": "update",
                    "done": true,
                    "verification": "Call each existing login, signup, and forgot-password endpoint with a first well-formed request and no device cookie, including failed credentials or an unknown recovery email: the response issues one device cookie and creates one device record. Repeat with that cookie and confirm no second device is created. A session is created only after successful login and survives a server restart; missing or mismatched device cookies invalidate access, while an IP change alone does not. Logout and password reset revoke sessions."
                },
                {
                    "id": "add-web-turnstile-to-auth-forms",
                    "title": "Add one reusable Cloudflare Turnstile component to the web login, signup, and forgot-password forms; send its proof as the platform-neutral verificationToken with verificationMethod set to turnstile, refresh expired or used tokens, and leave Android and iOS UI unchanged",
                    "version": "0.3.10",
                    "type": "frontend",
                    "changeType": "add",
                    "done": true,
                    "verification": "On the web, open login, signup, and forgot-password and confirm each form obtains a Turnstile token before submission, prevents duplicate submissions, and requests a fresh token after expiry or use. Confirm the existing POST paths and other request fields remain unchanged. Android and iOS do not display Turnstile."
                },
                {
                    "id": "verify-web-turnstile-before-device-access",
                    "title": "Verify the generic verificationToken using the turnstile verificationMethod on the existing login, signup, and forgot-password POST endpoints before looking up, creating, or updating a device; validate Cloudflare Siteverify success, expected action, and allowed hostname, with a separate verifier that can accept native methods later",
                    "version": "0.3.11",
                    "type": "backend",
